set-priority — Set the Priority field on an issue (optionally cascading to sub-issues).

  Purpose:       Set the Priority field on an issue (optionally cascading to sub-issues).
  Group:         GitHub
  Usage:         aitm set-priority <issue#> <p0|p1|p2|p3> [--cascade]
  Audience:      AI/operator setting priority. Priorities: p0|p1|p2|p3.
  Arguments:     <issue#>, <p0|p1|p2|p3>, --cascade
  Preconditions: AI/operator setting priority. Priorities: p0|p1|p2|p3.
  Effects:       Set the Priority field on an issue (optionally cascading to sub-issues).
  Output:        Prints each issue whose project Priority field was updated.
  Exit codes:    0=priority update completed; 1=usage, configuration, or GitHub update failed
  Examples:      npx aitm set-priority 1023 p1; npx aitm set-priority 1005 p2 --cascade
  Related:       set-rank, project-tether

Invoke via the package or orchestrator command name:
  npx aitm set-priority <issue#> <p0|p1|p2|p3> [--cascade]
